<map version="1.0.1">
<node ID="ID_2161" TEXT="Chapter 6 — Claude Code mastery (on your real project)"><richcontent TYPE="NOTE"><html><head></head><body><p>2026-10-12 → 2026-10-18</p><p>Claude Code</p></body></html></richcontent><node ID="ID_1876" TEXT="🎯 Goal"><richcontent TYPE="NOTE"><html><head></head><body><p>Turn daily Claude Code use into exam-grade knowledge of memory, settings, hooks, subagents, headless mode and CI. Only ~3% of the exam — keep it to the schedule and do not over-invest.</p></body></html></richcontent></node><node ID="ID_1878" TEXT="Exam domains"><node ID="ID_1877" TEXT="Claude Code — 3.1%"></node></node><node ID="ID_1954" TEXT="📅 Daily plan"><node ID="ID_1889" TEXT="10-12 · Memory hierarchy: CLAUDE.md at user / project / local levels, @impo…"><node ID="ID_1879" TEXT="Learn: Memory hierarchy: CLAUDE.md at user / project / local levels, @imports, settings.json precedence"></node><node ID="ID_1884" TEXT="Build: Write a proper project CLAUDE.md: stack, commands, conventions, review checklist"><node ID="ID_1880" TEXT="Run /init in your dev project; then rewrite CLAUDE.md by hand: stack, how to build/test/lint, conventions, what never to touch, PR checklist. Keep it under ~150 lines."></node><node ID="ID_1881" TEXT="Add @docs/architecture.md import; add a CLAUDE.local.md with a personal note and confirm it is git-ignored."></node><node ID="ID_1882" TEXT="Use /memory to see which files are loaded; ask Claude Code a question only CLAUDE.md answers to prove it is read."></node><node ID="ID_1883" TEXT="Read the settings precedence: managed (enterprise) &gt; command line &gt; .claude/settings.local.json &gt; .claude/settings.json &gt; ~/.claude/settings.json; write it in notes."></node></node><node ID="ID_1885" TEXT="✔ Done when: CLAUDE.md committed; import works; precedence order written from memory."></node><node ID="ID_1888" TEXT="Read"><node ID="ID_1886" TEXT="Claude Code: memory (CLAUDE.md)" LINK="https://docs.claude.com/en/docs/claude-code/memory"><richcontent TYPE="NOTE"><html><head></head><body><p>https://docs.claude.com/en/docs/claude-code/memory</p></body></html></richcontent></node><node ID="ID_1887" TEXT="Claude Code: settings" LINK="https://docs.claude.com/en/docs/claude-code/settings"><richcontent TYPE="NOTE"><html><head></head><body><p>https://docs.claude.com/en/docs/claude-code/settings</p></body></html></richcontent></node></node></node><node ID="ID_1900" TEXT="10-13 · Custom slash commands, Skills (.claude/skills), rules"><node ID="ID_1890" TEXT="Learn: Custom slash commands, Skills (.claude/skills), rules"></node><node ID="ID_1895" TEXT="Build: Add a /test command and a skill for your coding standard"><node ID="ID_1891" TEXT="Create .claude/commands/test.md with frontmatter (description, allowed-tools) and a body that runs the test suite and summarises failures; use $ARGUMENTS."></node><node ID="ID_1892" TEXT="Create .claude/skills/coding-standard/SKILL.md with a description that says when it applies; verify Claude Code applies it unprompted on a matching task."></node><node ID="ID_1893" TEXT="Note the differences: command = user-invoked, explicit; skill = model-invoked when relevant, can carry scripts/resources; CLAUDE.md = always loaded."></node><node ID="ID_1894" TEXT="List the built-in commands you use: /clear, /compact, /cost, /model, /permissions, /mcp, /memory, /init, /review, /help."></node></node><node ID="ID_1896" TEXT="✔ Done when: /test works with arguments; the skill triggers automatically; the three-way comparison is in notes."></node><node ID="ID_1899" TEXT="Read"><node ID="ID_1897" TEXT="Slash commands" LINK="https://docs.claude.com/en/docs/claude-code/slash-commands"><richcontent TYPE="NOTE"><html><head></head><body><p>https://docs.claude.com/en/docs/claude-code/slash-commands</p></body></html></richcontent></node><node ID="ID_1898" TEXT="Skills in Claude Code" LINK="https://docs.claude.com/en/docs/claude-code/skills"><richcontent TYPE="NOTE"><html><head></head><body><p>https://docs.claude.com/en/docs/claude-code/skills</p></body></html></richcontent></node></node></node><node ID="ID_1912" TEXT="10-14 · Hooks: PreToolUse / PostToolUse / Stop; permission modes; plan mode"><node ID="ID_1901" TEXT="Learn: Hooks: PreToolUse / PostToolUse / Stop; permission modes; plan mode"></node><node ID="ID_1906" TEXT="Build: Hook that runs the linter after every edit; do a plan-mode refactor"><node ID="ID_1902" TEXT="Add a PostToolUse hook matching Edit|Write that runs ruff/black on the changed file (read the file path from the hook's stdin JSON)."></node><node ID="ID_1903" TEXT="Add a PreToolUse hook on Bash that blocks commands containing 'terraform destroy' (exit code 2 blocks and feeds stderr back to Claude)."></node><node ID="ID_1904" TEXT="Try each permission mode: default, acceptEdits, plan, bypassPermissions (only in a container) — note what each allows."></node><node ID="ID_1905" TEXT="Do a real refactor in plan mode (Shift+Tab) and approve the plan before edits."></node></node><node ID="ID_1907" TEXT="✔ Done when: Both hooks fire and behave; you can explain exit code 2 vs 0 and the four modes."></node><node ID="ID_1911" TEXT="Read"><node ID="ID_1908" TEXT="Hooks reference" LINK="https://docs.claude.com/en/docs/claude-code/hooks"><richcontent TYPE="NOTE"><html><head></head><body><p>https://docs.claude.com/en/docs/claude-code/hooks</p></body></html></richcontent></node><node ID="ID_1909" TEXT="Hooks guide" LINK="https://docs.claude.com/en/docs/claude-code/hooks-guide"><richcontent TYPE="NOTE"><html><head></head><body><p>https://docs.claude.com/en/docs/claude-code/hooks-guide</p></body></html></richcontent></node><node ID="ID_1910" TEXT="Permissions / IAM" LINK="https://docs.claude.com/en/docs/claude-code/iam"><richcontent TYPE="NOTE"><html><head></head><body><p>https://docs.claude.com/en/docs/claude-code/iam</p></body></html></richcontent></node></node></node><node ID="ID_1922" TEXT="10-15 · Subagents (.claude/agents), when to delegate, context isolation"><node ID="ID_1913" TEXT="Learn: Subagents (.claude/agents), when to delegate, context isolation"></node><node ID="ID_1918" TEXT="Build: Create a reviewer subagent and use it on a PR"><node ID="ID_1914" TEXT="Use /agents to create .claude/agents/reviewer.md: frontmatter name, description (when to use it), tools (read-only), model; body = its system prompt."></node><node ID="ID_1915" TEXT="Ask Claude Code to 'use the reviewer subagent on the last PR' and watch it delegate; note that the main context stays clean."></node><node ID="ID_1916" TEXT="Compare project-level (.claude/agents) vs user-level (~/.claude/agents) subagents and precedence."></node><node ID="ID_1917" TEXT="Write when to delegate: long research, reviews, anything that would flood the main context."></node></node><node ID="ID_1919" TEXT="✔ Done when: Reviewer subagent exists, was invoked, and its scope/tools are restricted."></node><node ID="ID_1921" TEXT="Read"><node ID="ID_1920" TEXT="Subagents" LINK="https://docs.claude.com/en/docs/claude-code/sub-agents"><richcontent TYPE="NOTE"><html><head></head><body><p>https://docs.claude.com/en/docs/claude-code/sub-agents</p></body></html></richcontent></node></node></node><node ID="ID_1933" TEXT="10-16 · Headless: claude -p, --output-format json / stream-json, CI usage, …"><node ID="ID_1923" TEXT="Learn: Headless: claude -p, --output-format json / stream-json, CI usage, /cost, /compact, /clear"></node><node ID="ID_1928" TEXT="Build: GitHub Actions job: on PR run claude -p 'review this diff'"><node ID="ID_1924" TEXT="Run claude -p &quot;summarise the last 3 commits&quot; --output-format json; parse the JSON (result, cost_usd, usage, session_id)."></node><node ID="ID_1925" TEXT="Try --output-format stream-json for streaming and --allowedTools to restrict; pipe a diff in via stdin."></node><node ID="ID_1926" TEXT="Install the Claude GitHub app (/install-github-app) or add the anthropics/claude-code-action workflow; store ANTHROPIC_API_KEY as a repo secret; open a PR and get a review comment."></node><node ID="ID_1927" TEXT="Write the /compact vs /clear rule and what /cost shows (session tokens and USD)."></node></node><node ID="ID_1929" TEXT="✔ Done when: Headless JSON run parsed; PR review posted by the Action."></node><node ID="ID_1932" TEXT="Read"><node ID="ID_1930" TEXT="Claude Code CLI reference" LINK="https://docs.claude.com/en/docs/claude-code/cli-reference"><richcontent TYPE="NOTE"><html><head></head><body><p>https://docs.claude.com/en/docs/claude-code/cli-reference</p></body></html></richcontent></node><node ID="ID_1931" TEXT="Claude Code GitHub Actions" LINK="https://docs.claude.com/en/docs/claude-code/github-actions"><richcontent TYPE="NOTE"><html><head></head><body><p>https://docs.claude.com/en/docs/claude-code/github-actions</p></body></html></richcontent></node></node></node><node ID="ID_1944" TEXT="10-17 · Git workflow with Claude Code: commits, PRs, worktrees, GitHub app;…"><node ID="ID_1934" TEXT="Learn: Git workflow with Claude Code: commits, PRs, worktrees, GitHub app; IDE integration"></node><node ID="ID_1939" TEXT="Build: Let Claude Code open a PR end to end"><node ID="ID_1935" TEXT="From a task description, let Claude Code branch, implement, run tests, commit with a good message, and open the PR with gh."></node><node ID="ID_1936" TEXT="Use git worktrees to run two Claude Code sessions on separate branches in parallel."></node><node ID="ID_1937" TEXT="Install the VS Code extension; try inline diffs and selection context."></node><node ID="ID_1938" TEXT="Note the security posture: it only sees the folder you start it in; permissions gate writes and commands; network access only via tools you allow."></node></node><node ID="ID_1940" TEXT="✔ Done when: PR opened end to end by Claude Code; worktree parallel session tried."></node><node ID="ID_1943" TEXT="Read"><node ID="ID_1941" TEXT="Common workflows" LINK="https://docs.claude.com/en/docs/claude-code/common-workflows"><richcontent TYPE="NOTE"><html><head></head><body><p>https://docs.claude.com/en/docs/claude-code/common-workflows</p></body></html></richcontent></node><node ID="ID_1942" TEXT="IDE integrations" LINK="https://docs.claude.com/en/docs/claude-code/ide-integrations"><richcontent TYPE="NOTE"><html><head></head><body><p>https://docs.claude.com/en/docs/claude-code/ide-integrations</p></body></html></richcontent></node></node></node><node ID="ID_1953" TEXT="10-18 · Review day"><node ID="ID_1945" TEXT="Learn: Review day"></node><node ID="ID_1949" TEXT="Build: Write notes/claude-code.md"><node ID="ID_1946" TEXT="Finish notes/claude-code.md: memory hierarchy, settings precedence, commands vs skills vs CLAUDE.md, hooks table, permission modes, subagents, headless flags, CI."></node><node ID="ID_1947" TEXT="Self-check; then the Claude Code quiz in the Question bank."></node><node ID="ID_1948" TEXT="Weekly retrospective."></node></node><node ID="ID_1950" TEXT="✔ Done when: Notes committed; quiz recorded; retrospective filled."></node><node ID="ID_1952" TEXT="Read"><node ID="ID_1951" TEXT="Study material below"></node></node></node></node><node ID="ID_1998" TEXT="📖 Study material"><node ID="ID_1957" TEXT="Memory files"><node ID="ID_1955" TEXT="Hierarchy, all loaded together: ~/.claude/CLAUDE.md (you, every project) → ./CLAUDE.md…"><richcontent TYPE="NOTE"><html><head></head><body><p>Hierarchy, all loaded together: ~/.claude/CLAUDE.md (you, every project) → ./CLAUDE.md (project, committed, team) → ./CLAUDE.local.md (you, this project, git-ignored). Parent-directory CLAUDE.md files load too; subdirectory ones load on demand. Enterprise/managed policy files sit above all.</p></body></html></richcontent></node><node ID="ID_1956" TEXT="@path/to/file imports other files; keep CLAUDE.md short and operational…"><richcontent TYPE="NOTE"><html><head></head><body><p>@path/to/file imports other files; keep CLAUDE.md short and operational (build/test/lint commands, conventions, what not to touch). /memory shows what is loaded; /init bootstraps one.</p></body></html></richcontent></node></node><node ID="ID_1964" TEXT="Settings precedence (highest first)"><node ID="ID_1958" TEXT="Managed/enterprise policy settings"></node><node ID="ID_1959" TEXT="Command-line flags"></node><node ID="ID_1960" TEXT=".claude/settings.local.json (personal, git-ignored)"></node><node ID="ID_1961" TEXT=".claude/settings.json (project, committed)"></node><node ID="ID_1962" TEXT="~/.claude/settings.json (user)"></node><node ID="ID_1963" TEXT="Settings hold permissions (allow/ask/deny rules per tool, e.g. Bash(npm run test:*)),…"><richcontent TYPE="NOTE"><html><head></head><body><p>Settings hold permissions (allow/ask/deny rules per tool, e.g. Bash(npm run test:*)), hooks, env vars, model defaults, MCP approvals.</p></body></html></richcontent></node></node><node ID="ID_1972" TEXT="Extending Claude Code"><node ID="ID_1965" TEXT="CLAUDE.md"><richcontent TYPE="NOTE"><html><head></head><body><p>project/user · always loaded · conventions, commands, context</p></body></html></richcontent></node><node ID="ID_1966" TEXT="Slash command"><richcontent TYPE="NOTE"><html><head></head><body><p>.claude/commands/*.md (legacy — a same-named skill wins) · user types /name · repeatable prompts with $ARGUMENTS / $0 $1, frontmatter allowed-tools</p></body></html></richcontent></node><node ID="ID_1967" TEXT="Skill"><richcontent TYPE="NOTE"><html><head></head><body><p>.claude/skills/&lt;name&gt;/SKILL.md · model, when description matches · procedures plus scripts/resources; progressive loading</p></body></html></richcontent></node><node ID="ID_1968" TEXT="Hook"><richcontent TYPE="NOTE"><html><head></head><body><p>settings.json · lifecycle event · deterministic enforcement: format, lint, block, notify</p></body></html></richcontent></node><node ID="ID_1969" TEXT="Subagent"><richcontent TYPE="NOTE"><html><head></head><body><p>.claude/agents/*.md · model delegates or user asks · isolated context, restricted tools, specialised role</p></body></html></richcontent></node><node ID="ID_1970" TEXT="MCP server"><richcontent TYPE="NOTE"><html><head></head><body><p>.mcp.json / claude mcp add · model calls tools · external systems</p></body></html></richcontent></node><node ID="ID_1971" TEXT="Plugin"><richcontent TYPE="NOTE"><html><head></head><body><p>marketplace · install · bundle of commands, skills, agents, hooks, MCP</p></body></html></richcontent></node></node><node ID="ID_1976" TEXT="Hooks"><node ID="ID_1973" TEXT="Events: PreToolUse, PostToolUse, Notification, UserPromptSubmit, Stop, SubagentStop,…"><richcontent TYPE="NOTE"><html><head></head><body><p>Events: PreToolUse, PostToolUse, Notification, UserPromptSubmit, Stop, SubagentStop, SessionStart, PreCompact and more. Matchers select tools (e.g. Edit|Write).</p></body></html></richcontent></node><node ID="ID_1974" TEXT="A hook is a shell command that receives JSON on stdin (tool name, input, file paths,…"><richcontent TYPE="NOTE"><html><head></head><body><p>A hook is a shell command that receives JSON on stdin (tool name, input, file paths, session). Exit 0 = continue; exit 2 = block and show stderr to Claude; other codes = non-blocking error. Hooks can also return JSON to allow/deny or add context.</p></body></html></richcontent></node><node ID="ID_1975" TEXT="Hooks are enforcement; CLAUDE.md is guidance. &quot;Must always/never&quot; → hook."></node></node><node ID="ID_1980" TEXT="Permissions and modes"><node ID="ID_1977" TEXT="default: reads free, asks before edits and commands. acceptEdits: file edits…"><richcontent TYPE="NOTE"><html><head></head><body><p>default: reads free, asks before edits and commands. acceptEdits: file edits auto-approved. plan: read-only, produces a plan for approval. auto: a classifier decides. dontAsk. bypassPermissions (--dangerously-skip-permissions): everything auto — only inside a sandbox/container without credentials; admins can disable it.</p></body></html></richcontent></node><node ID="ID_1978" TEXT="Rules evaluate deny → ask → allow, first match wins; a broad deny beats a narrow…"><richcontent TYPE="NOTE"><html><head></head><body><p>Rules evaluate deny → ask → allow, first match wins; a broad deny beats a narrow allow. Committed project allow rules wait for workspace trust; deny applies immediately. In -p mode trust checks are skipped — restrict tools explicitly.</p></body></html></richcontent></node><node ID="ID_1979" TEXT="Allow-list patterns in settings; /permissions to manage; deny rules win."></node></node><node ID="ID_1983" TEXT="Subagents"><node ID="ID_1981" TEXT="Markdown files with frontmatter (name, description — used for automatic delegation,…"><richcontent TYPE="NOTE"><html><head></head><body><p>Markdown files with frontmatter (name, description — used for automatic delegation, tools, model) and a system prompt body. Project-level overrides user-level with the same name.</p></body></html></richcontent></node><node ID="ID_1982" TEXT="Run in a separate context window; return a summary. Good for reviews, research,…"><richcontent TYPE="NOTE"><html><head></head><body><p>Run in a separate context window; return a summary. Good for reviews, research, test-writing; cost extra tokens and lose the main thread's context.</p></body></html></richcontent></node></node><node ID="ID_1993" TEXT="Headless and CI"><node ID="ID_1984" TEXT="claude -p &quot;prompt&quot; non-interactive; --output-format text|json|stream-json;…"><richcontent TYPE="NOTE"><html><head></head><body><p>claude -p &quot;prompt&quot; non-interactive; --output-format text|json|stream-json; --allowedTools, --max-turns, --model, --resume &lt;session&gt;, --continue. JSON output includes result, cost, usage, session_id.</p></body></html></richcontent></node><node ID="ID_1985" TEXT="GitHub Actions: anthropics/claude-code-action — @claude in issues/PRs, automated…"><richcontent TYPE="NOTE"><html><head></head><body><p>GitHub Actions: anthropics/claude-code-action — @claude in issues/PRs, automated review; API key from secrets; also works with Bedrock/Vertex credentials.</p></body></html></richcontent></node><node ID="ID_1986" TEXT="Session commands: /compact [focus] summarises context and keeps going; /clear wipes…"><richcontent TYPE="NOTE"><html><head></head><body><p>Session commands: /compact [focus] summarises context and keeps going; /clear wipes it; /cost (alias of /usage) shows tokens and USD; /context shows what is loaded; /model, /effort; /review (alias of /code-review); /resume, /fork, /rewind for sessions.</p></body></html></richcontent></node><node ID="ID_1992" TEXT="⚠ Exam traps"><node ID="ID_1987" TEXT="CLAUDE.md is guidance, hooks are enforcement — pick hooks for &quot;must always&quot;. /compact summarises the context, /clear wipes it."></node><node ID="ID_1988" TEXT="Subagents cost extra tokens because they have their own context."></node><node ID="ID_1989" TEXT="Project settings.json is shared; settings.local.json is personal and outranks it; CLI flags outrank both; managed outranks everything."></node><node ID="ID_1990" TEXT="Exit code 2 in a hook blocks (exit 1 does not). bypassPermissions is for sandboxes only."></node><node ID="ID_1991" TEXT="Project agents beat user agents, but personal skills beat project skills."></node></node></node><node ID="ID_1995" TEXT="Hook example (settings.json)"><node ID="ID_1994" TEXT="{ } code sample"><richcontent TYPE="NOTE"><html><head></head><body><p>{</p><p>  &quot;hooks&quot;: {</p><p>    &quot;PostToolUse&quot;: [{</p><p>      &quot;matcher&quot;: &quot;Edit|Write&quot;,</p><p>      &quot;hooks&quot;: [{&quot;type&quot;:&quot;command&quot;,&quot;command&quot;:&quot;jq -r '.tool_input.file_path' | xargs -I{} ruff format {}&quot;}]</p><p>    }],</p><p>    &quot;PreToolUse&quot;: [{</p><p>      &quot;matcher&quot;: &quot;Bash&quot;,</p><p>      &quot;hooks&quot;: [{&quot;type&quot;:&quot;command&quot;,&quot;command&quot;:&quot;jq -r .tool_input.command | grep -q 'terraform destroy' &amp;&amp; { echo 'blocked: destroy' &gt;&amp;2; exit 2; } || exit 0&quot;}]</p><p>    }]</p><p>  }</p><p>}</p></body></html></richcontent></node></node><node ID="ID_1997" TEXT="Subagent file"><node ID="ID_1996" TEXT="{ } code sample"><richcontent TYPE="NOTE"><html><head></head><body><p>---</p><p>name: reviewer</p><p>description: Reviews code changes for error handling and security. Use after any edit to src/.</p><p>tools: Read, Grep, Glob</p><p>model: sonnet</p><p>---</p><p>You are a strict reviewer. Report findings with file:line. Never edit files.</p></body></html></richcontent></node></node></node><node ID="ID_2110" TEXT="📚 Library digests"><node ID="ID_2012" TEXT="Claude Code — memory (CLAUDE.md, rules, auto memory)" LINK="https://code.claude.com/docs/en/memory"><richcontent TYPE="NOTE"><html><head></head><body><p>https://code.claude.com/docs/en/memory</p></body></html></richcontent><node ID="ID_2006" TEXT="Key facts"><node ID="ID_1999" TEXT="Two memory systems: CLAUDE.md (you write) and auto memory (Claude writes). Both are…"><richcontent TYPE="NOTE"><html><head></head><body><p>Two memory systems: CLAUDE.md (you write) and auto memory (Claude writes). Both are context/guidance, not enforcement — use a PreToolUse hook to hard-block.</p></body></html></richcontent></node><node ID="ID_2000" TEXT="Load order: managed policy CLAUDE.md (OS-level path) → user ~/.claude/CLAUDE.md → project…"><richcontent TYPE="NOTE"><html><head></head><body><p>Load order: managed policy CLAUDE.md (OS-level path) → user ~/.claude/CLAUDE.md → project ./CLAUDE.md or ./.claude/CLAUDE.md → local ./CLAUDE.local.md (git-ignore it). Files in the cwd and every ancestor load at launch (closer files read last); subdirectory CLAUDE.md loads on demand when Claude reads files there.</p></body></html></richcontent></node><node ID="ID_2001" TEXT="Imports: @path/to/file (relative or absolute), max depth 4 hops; imports inside code fences are…"><richcontent TYPE="NOTE"><html><head></head><body><p>Imports: @path/to/file (relative or absolute), max depth 4 hops; imports inside code fences are ignored; imports outside the working directory prompt once.</p></body></html></richcontent></node><node ID="ID_2002" TEXT="Size: target under 200 lines; a CLAUDE.md over 4 MiB is skipped. HTML comments are stripped."></node><node ID="ID_2003" TEXT=".claude/rules/*.md: rules without paths: frontmatter load at launch; with paths: globs they load…"><richcontent TYPE="NOTE"><html><head></head><body><p>.claude/rules/*.md: rules without paths: frontmatter load at launch; with paths: globs they load only when Claude touches matching files — this is what actually saves context (imports do not).</p></body></html></richcontent></node><node ID="ID_2004" TEXT="Auto memory: on by default (autoMemoryEnabled:false or CLAUDE_CODE_DISABLE_AUTO_MEMORY=1 to…"><richcontent TYPE="NOTE"><html><head></head><body><p>Auto memory: on by default (autoMemoryEnabled:false or CLAUDE_CODE_DISABLE_AUTO_MEMORY=1 to disable); stored under ~/.claude/projects/&lt;project&gt;/memory/ with MEMORY.md index; only the first 200 lines / 25 KB of MEMORY.md loads; not loaded into subagents (except forks).</p></body></html></richcontent></node><node ID="ID_2005" TEXT="/init generates CLAUDE.md; /memory edits memory files; /context shows what actually loaded.…"><richcontent TYPE="NOTE"><html><head></head><body><p>/init generates CLAUDE.md; /memory edits memory files; /context shows what actually loaded. Claude reads CLAUDE.md, not AGENTS.md (import it with @AGENTS.md). Project-root CLAUDE.md survives /compact.</p></body></html></richcontent></node></node><node ID="ID_2010" TEXT="⚠ Exam traps"><node ID="ID_2007" TEXT="Import depth is 4 hops; @README inside backticks does not import."></node><node ID="ID_2008" TEXT="Managed CLAUDE.md cannot be excluded by claudeMdExcludes."></node><node ID="ID_2009" TEXT="Splitting into @imports does not save context; path-scoped .claude/rules/ does."></node></node><node ID="ID_2011" TEXT="{ } code"><richcontent TYPE="NOTE"><html><head></head><body><p>---</p><p>paths:</p><p>  - &quot;src/api/**/*.ts&quot;</p><p>---</p><p># API rules</p><p>- All endpoints must validate input with zod</p><p>- Never log request bodies</p></body></html></richcontent></node></node><node ID="ID_2026" TEXT="Claude Code — settings and precedence" LINK="https://code.claude.com/docs/en/settings"><richcontent TYPE="NOTE"><html><head></head><body><p>https://code.claude.com/docs/en/settings</p></body></html></richcontent><node ID="ID_2020" TEXT="Key facts"><node ID="ID_2013" TEXT="Files: user ~/.claude/settings.json; shared project .claude/settings.json; project local…"><richcontent TYPE="NOTE"><html><head></head><body><p>Files: user ~/.claude/settings.json; shared project .claude/settings.json; project local .claude/settings.local.json (auto-gitignored); managed managed-settings.json (OS-level path / MDM / console). ~/.claude.json holds global config, sign-in, MCP servers, trust decisions.</p></body></html></richcontent></node><node ID="ID_2014" TEXT="Precedence, highest first: 1 Managed → 2 Command line (--settings, flags) → 3 Project local → 4…"><richcontent TYPE="NOTE"><html><head></head><body><p>Precedence, highest first: 1 Managed → 2 Command line (--settings, flags) → 3 Project local → 4 Shared project → 5 User.</p></body></html></richcontent></node><node ID="ID_2015" TEXT="List keys (e.g. permissions.allow) MERGE across files; a few keys take the whole value from the…"><richcontent TYPE="NOTE"><html><head></head><body><p>List keys (e.g. permissions.allow) MERGE across files; a few keys take the whole value from the highest layer (fallbackModel, availableModels).</p></body></html></richcontent></node><node ID="ID_2016" TEXT="Env vars are not a layer: ANTHROPIC_MODEL overrides model from any file; --model overrides…"><richcontent TYPE="NOTE"><html><head></head><body><p>Env vars are not a layer: ANTHROPIC_MODEL overrides model from any file; --model overrides everything.</p></body></html></richcontent></node><node ID="ID_2017" TEXT="permissions.defaultMode values auto and bypassPermissions are ignored from project/local…"><richcontent TYPE="NOTE"><html><head></head><body><p>permissions.defaultMode values auto and bypassPermissions are ignored from project/local settings (user/managed only).</p></body></html></richcontent></node><node ID="ID_2018" TEXT="Committed permissions.allow, additionalDirectories and most env values wait for workspace trust;…"><richcontent TYPE="NOTE"><html><head></head><body><p>Committed permissions.allow, additionalDirectories and most env values wait for workspace trust; deny/ask apply immediately. A local allow does not outrank a project/managed ask.</p></body></html></richcontent></node><node ID="ID_2019" TEXT="Strict JSON (no comments); '$schema': https://json.schemastore.org/claude-code-settings.json.…"><richcontent TYPE="NOTE"><html><head></head><body><p>Strict JSON (no comments); '$schema': https://json.schemastore.org/claude-code-settings.json. Permissions and hooks hot-reload; model/effort are read at start (use /model, /effort). 'Yes, don't ask again' writes an allow rule to .claude/settings.local.json.</p></body></html></richcontent></node></node><node ID="ID_2024" TEXT="⚠ Exam traps"><node ID="ID_2021" TEXT="--settings on the command line beats project/local/user files but never managed."></node><node ID="ID_2022" TEXT="settings.local.json outranks the committed settings.json, but list keys merge rather than replace."></node><node ID="ID_2023" TEXT="bypassPermissions as defaultMode in .claude/settings.json is silently ignored."></node></node><node ID="ID_2025" TEXT="{ } code"><richcontent TYPE="NOTE"><html><head></head><body><p>{</p><p>  &quot;$schema&quot;: &quot;https://json.schemastore.org/claude-code-settings.json&quot;,</p><p>  &quot;permissions&quot;: {</p><p>    &quot;allow&quot;: [&quot;Bash(npm run lint)&quot;, &quot;Bash(npm run test *)&quot;],</p><p>    &quot;deny&quot;:  [&quot;Read(./.env)&quot;, &quot;Read(./.env.*)&quot;, &quot;Bash(terraform destroy *)&quot;]</p><p>  }</p><p>}</p></body></html></richcontent></node></node><node ID="ID_2041" TEXT="Claude Code — skills and slash commands" LINK="https://code.claude.com/docs/en/skills"><richcontent TYPE="NOTE"><html><head></head><body><p>https://code.claude.com/docs/en/skills</p></body></html></richcontent><node ID="ID_2034" TEXT="Key facts"><node ID="ID_2027" TEXT="Custom slash commands (.claude/commands/&lt;name&gt;.md, invoked as /name) still work but are legacy;…"><richcontent TYPE="NOTE"><html><head></head><body><p>Custom slash commands (.claude/commands/&lt;name&gt;.md, invoked as /name) still work but are legacy; skills (.claude/skills/&lt;name&gt;/SKILL.md) are the recommended form and WIN on a name collision.</p></body></html></richcontent></node><node ID="ID_2028" TEXT="Skill = YAML frontmatter + Markdown body. Frontmatter: description (+ when_to_use),…"><richcontent TYPE="NOTE"><html><head></head><body><p>Skill = YAML frontmatter + Markdown body. Frontmatter: description (+ when_to_use), argument-hint, allowed-tools, disallowed-tools, model, effort, context: fork, agent, background, paths, disable-model-invocation, user-invocable.</p></body></html></richcontent></node><node ID="ID_2029" TEXT="Invocation control: default = you or Claude can invoke; disable-model-invocation:true = only you…"><richcontent TYPE="NOTE"><html><head></head><body><p>Invocation control: default = you or Claude can invoke; disable-model-invocation:true = only you (description hidden from Claude); user-invocable:false = only Claude (hidden from the / menu).</p></body></html></richcontent></node><node ID="ID_2030" TEXT="Arguments: $ARGUMENTS (all), $0 / $1 positional (0-based), named via arguments: frontmatter.…"><richcontent TYPE="NOTE"><html><head></head><body><p>Arguments: $ARGUMENTS (all), $0 / $1 positional (0-based), named via arguments: frontmatter. Shell injection with !`cmd` runs before Claude sees the content (needs allowed-tools; 2-min timeout).</p></body></html></richcontent></node><node ID="ID_2031" TEXT="Locations/precedence: Enterprise &gt; Personal ~/.claude/skills &gt; Project .claude/skills &gt; Plugin &gt;…"><richcontent TYPE="NOTE"><html><head></head><body><p>Locations/precedence: Enterprise &gt; Personal ~/.claude/skills &gt; Project .claude/skills &gt; Plugin &gt; bundled. context: fork runs the skill in an isolated subagent; paths: auto-loads only for matching files.</p></body></html></richcontent></node><node ID="ID_2032" TEXT="allowed-tools in a skill is a one-turn grant, not a persistent rule. Compaction keeps the most…"><richcontent TYPE="NOTE"><html><head></head><body><p>allowed-tools in a skill is a one-turn grant, not a persistent rule. Compaction keeps the most recent skills (≈5k tokens each, 25k combined).</p></body></html></richcontent></node><node ID="ID_2033" TEXT="Built-in commands: /clear (/reset, /new), /compact [instructions], /config, /context, /usage…"><richcontent TYPE="NOTE"><html><head></head><body><p>Built-in commands: /clear (/reset, /new), /compact [instructions], /config, /context, /usage (alias /cost), /init, /memory, /model, /effort, /permissions, /status, /rewind, /resume, /agents, /hooks, /mcp, /plugin, /export, /add-dir, /plan, /code-review (/review), /security-review, /install-github-app, /tasks, /fork. MCP prompts appear as /mcp__server__prompt.</p></body></html></richcontent></node></node><node ID="ID_2038" TEXT="⚠ Exam traps"><node ID="ID_2035" TEXT="Positional args are 0-based ($0 is the first)."></node><node ID="ID_2036" TEXT=".claude/commands/ is legacy; if a skill and a command share a name, the skill wins."></node><node ID="ID_2037" TEXT="/cost is now an alias of /usage; /review is an alias of /code-review."></node></node><node ID="ID_2039" TEXT="Then vs now"><richcontent TYPE="NOTE"><html><head></head><body><p>The blueprint lists 'Rules, Skills, Commands, Agents, Agent Memory' as separate components — answer with that taxonomy (command = user-invoked prompt; skill = model-invoked know-how) even though the docs have merged the implementations.</p></body></html></richcontent></node><node ID="ID_2040" TEXT="{ } code"><richcontent TYPE="NOTE"><html><head></head><body><p>---</p><p>description: Run the test suite and summarise failures. Use after code changes.</p><p>argument-hint: [test-path]</p><p>allowed-tools: Bash(pytest *)</p><p>---</p><p>Test output: !`pytest $0 -q 2&gt;&amp;1 | tail -40`</p><p>Summarise failures with file:line and the likely cause.</p></body></html></richcontent></node></node><node ID="ID_2055" TEXT="Claude Code — hooks reference" LINK="https://code.claude.com/docs/en/hooks"><richcontent TYPE="NOTE"><html><head></head><body><p>https://code.claude.com/docs/en/hooks</p></body></html></richcontent><node ID="ID_2049" TEXT="Key facts"><node ID="ID_2042" TEXT="Events (selection): SessionStart, SessionEnd, UserPromptSubmit, PreToolUse, PostToolUse,…"><richcontent TYPE="NOTE"><html><head></head><body><p>Events (selection): SessionStart, SessionEnd, UserPromptSubmit, PreToolUse, PostToolUse, PostToolUseFailure, PermissionRequest, Stop, SubagentStart, SubagentStop, PreCompact, PostCompact, Notification, ConfigChange, FileChanged…</p></body></html></richcontent></node><node ID="ID_2043" TEXT="Handler types: command (JSON on stdin → stdout), http (POST), mcp_tool, prompt (single-turn…"><richcontent TYPE="NOTE"><html><head></head><body><p>Handler types: command (JSON on stdin → stdout), http (POST), mcp_tool, prompt (single-turn model evaluation), agent.</p></body></html></richcontent></node><node ID="ID_2044" TEXT="Structure: hooks.&lt;Event&gt;[] = {matcher, hooks:[{type, command, timeout, async, if}]}. Matchers:…"><richcontent TYPE="NOTE"><html><head></head><body><p>Structure: hooks.&lt;Event&gt;[] = {matcher, hooks:[{type, command, timeout, async, if}]}. Matchers: exact tool names, A|B alternatives, regex (e.g. mcp__memory__.*), * or omitted = all. if uses permission-rule syntax such as Bash(rm *).</p></body></html></richcontent></node><node ID="ID_2045" TEXT="Timeouts: default 600 s for command/http/mcp_tool, 30 s prompt; on timeout PreToolUse does NOT…"><richcontent TYPE="NOTE"><html><head></head><body><p>Timeouts: default 600 s for command/http/mcp_tool, 30 s prompt; on timeout PreToolUse does NOT block.</p></body></html></richcontent></node><node ID="ID_2046" TEXT="Exit codes: 0 = proceed (stdout parsed as JSON if it starts with '{'); 2 = BLOCK (stderr shown…"><richcontent TYPE="NOTE"><html><head></head><body><p>Exit codes: 0 = proceed (stdout parsed as JSON if it starts with '{'); 2 = BLOCK (stderr shown to Claude as the reason; PreToolUse blocks the tool, UserPromptSubmit rejects the prompt); any other code = non-blocking error, action proceeds.</p></body></html></richcontent></node><node ID="ID_2047" TEXT="Stdin JSON: session_id, cwd, permission_mode, hook_event_name, tool_name, tool_input,…"><richcontent TYPE="NOTE"><html><head></head><body><p>Stdin JSON: session_id, cwd, permission_mode, hook_event_name, tool_name, tool_input, tool_use_id… JSON output can set continue, stopReason, systemMessage, additionalContext, hookSpecificOutput.permissionDecision allow|deny|ask, updatedInput.</p></body></html></richcontent></node><node ID="ID_2048" TEXT="Where: user/project/local settings, managed settings, plugin hooks/hooks.json, skill/subagent…"><richcontent TYPE="NOTE"><html><head></head><body><p>Where: user/project/local settings, managed settings, plugin hooks/hooks.json, skill/subagent frontmatter. Project/local hooks wait for workspace trust; disableAllHooks:true does not disable managed hooks; /hooks is a read-only viewer.</p></body></html></richcontent></node></node><node ID="ID_2053" TEXT="⚠ Exam traps"><node ID="ID_2050" TEXT="Exit 2 blocks; exit 1 does not (non-blocking error, action proceeds)."></node><node ID="ID_2051" TEXT="Default command-hook timeout is 600 s, not 60."></node><node ID="ID_2052" TEXT="disableAllHooks cannot disable managed-settings hooks."></node></node><node ID="ID_2054" TEXT="{ } code"><richcontent TYPE="NOTE"><html><head></head><body><p>{</p><p>  &quot;hooks&quot;: {</p><p>    &quot;PostToolUse&quot;: [{&quot;matcher&quot;: &quot;Edit|Write&quot;,</p><p>      &quot;hooks&quot;: [{&quot;type&quot;:&quot;command&quot;,&quot;command&quot;:&quot;jq -r .tool_input.file_path | xargs ruff format&quot;}]}],</p><p>    &quot;PreToolUse&quot;: [{&quot;matcher&quot;: &quot;Bash&quot;,</p><p>      &quot;hooks&quot;: [{&quot;type&quot;:&quot;command&quot;,&quot;if&quot;:&quot;Bash(terraform destroy *)&quot;,</p><p>                 &quot;command&quot;:&quot;echo 'blocked: destroy needs a human' &gt;&amp;2; exit 2&quot;}]}]</p><p>  }</p><p>}</p></body></html></richcontent></node></node><node ID="ID_2069" TEXT="Claude Code — permissions, modes and authentication" LINK="https://code.claude.com/docs/en/permissions"><richcontent TYPE="NOTE"><html><head></head><body><p>https://code.claude.com/docs/en/permissions</p></body></html></richcontent><node ID="ID_2063" TEXT="Key facts"><node ID="ID_2056" TEXT="Rule evaluation: deny → ask → allow, first match wins; a broad deny beats a narrow allow (deny…"><richcontent TYPE="NOTE"><html><head></head><body><p>Rule evaluation: deny → ask → allow, first match wins; a broad deny beats a narrow allow (deny rules can't carry exceptions).</p></body></html></richcontent></node><node ID="ID_2057" TEXT="Modes: default (manual: reads free, asks before edits/commands), acceptEdits, plan (read-only,…"><richcontent TYPE="NOTE"><html><head></head><body><p>Modes: default (manual: reads free, asks before edits/commands), acceptEdits, plan (read-only, proposes), auto (classifier decides), dontAsk, bypassPermissions (--dangerously-skip-permissions; sandboxes only; can be disabled by admins).</p></body></html></richcontent></node><node ID="ID_2058" TEXT="Bash rules: Bash(npm run *) matches 'npm run …'; Bash(ls *) excludes lsof; compound commands…"><richcontent TYPE="NOTE"><html><head></head><body><p>Bash rules: Bash(npm run *) matches 'npm run …'; Bash(ls *) excludes lsof; compound commands (&amp;&amp;, ||, ;, |) are split and each part must match; wrappers like timeout/nice are stripped; suspicious commands prompt even if allow-listed.</p></body></html></richcontent></node><node ID="ID_2059" TEXT="File rules use gitignore syntax: Read(./.env), //absolute, ~/home; a Read deny also blocks…"><richcontent TYPE="NOTE"><html><head></head><body><p>File rules use gitignore syntax: Read(./.env), //absolute, ~/home; a Read deny also blocks Edit/Write on that path. WebFetch(domain:host); mcp__server = all tools on it; mcp__server__tool = one; Agent(Explore).</p></body></html></richcontent></node><node ID="ID_2060" TEXT="Committed project allow rules and additionalDirectories wait for workspace trust; deny/ask apply…"><richcontent TYPE="NOTE"><html><head></head><body><p>Committed project allow rules and additionalDirectories wait for workspace trust; deny/ask apply immediately. Trust verification is skipped in -p mode.</p></body></html></richcontent></node><node ID="ID_2061" TEXT="Credential precedence: cloud provider env (CLAUDE_CODE_USE_BEDROCK|VERTEX|FOUNDRY) →…"><richcontent TYPE="NOTE"><html><head></head><body><p>Credential precedence: cloud provider env (CLAUDE_CODE_USE_BEDROCK|VERTEX|FOUNDRY) → ANTHROPIC_AUTH_TOKEN → ANTHROPIC_API_KEY → apiKeyHelper (re-run every 5 min) → CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN (claude setup-token, one-year, for CI) → profile/WIF → /login OAuth. Stored in macOS Keychain or ~/.claude/.credentials.json (0600).</p></body></html></richcontent></node><node ID="ID_2062" TEXT="Security posture: writes only under the start folder; network commands (curl, wget) not…"><richcontent TYPE="NOTE"><html><head></head><body><p>Security posture: writes only under the start folder; network commands (curl, wget) not auto-approved; web-fetched content is processed in an isolated context (injection mitigation); MCP servers are not audited by Anthropic; report vulnerabilities via HackerOne.</p></body></html></richcontent></node></node><node ID="ID_2067" TEXT="⚠ Exam traps"><node ID="ID_2064" TEXT="ANTHROPIC_API_KEY outranks a /login subscription once approved; ANTHROPIC_AUTH_TOKEN outranks the API key."></node><node ID="ID_2065" TEXT="deny Bash(aws *) blocks Bash(aws s3 ls) even if that is allowed."></node><node ID="ID_2066" TEXT="Trust verification and prompts are skipped in -p (headless) mode — restrict tools explicitly there."></node></node><node ID="ID_2068" TEXT="{ } code"><richcontent TYPE="NOTE"><html><head></head><body><p>{</p><p>  &quot;permissions&quot;: {</p><p>    &quot;allow&quot;: [&quot;Bash(npm run *)&quot;, &quot;Bash(git commit *)&quot;, &quot;WebFetch(domain:github.com)&quot;],</p><p>    &quot;ask&quot;:   [&quot;Bash(git clean *)&quot;],</p><p>    &quot;deny&quot;:  [&quot;Bash(git push *)&quot;, &quot;Read(./.env)&quot;, &quot;Bash(curl *)&quot;],</p><p>    &quot;disableBypassPermissionsMode&quot;: &quot;disable&quot;</p><p>  }</p><p>}</p></body></html></richcontent></node></node><node ID="ID_2082" TEXT="Claude Code — subagents" LINK="https://code.claude.com/docs/en/sub-agents"><richcontent TYPE="NOTE"><html><head></head><body><p>https://code.claude.com/docs/en/sub-agents</p></body></html></richcontent><node ID="ID_2076" TEXT="Key facts"><node ID="ID_2070" TEXT="Files = YAML frontmatter + Markdown system prompt. Priority: managed &gt; --agents CLI JSON &gt;…"><richcontent TYPE="NOTE"><html><head></head><body><p>Files = YAML frontmatter + Markdown system prompt. Priority: managed &gt; --agents CLI JSON &gt; project .claude/agents/ &gt; user ~/.claude/agents/ &gt; plugin agents. Closest project file wins; live-reloaded.</p></body></html></richcontent></node><node ID="ID_2071" TEXT="Required frontmatter: name, description (drives automatic delegation). Optional: tools…"><richcontent TYPE="NOTE"><html><head></head><body><p>Required frontmatter: name, description (drives automatic delegation). Optional: tools (allow-list), disallowedTools, model (sonnet | opus | haiku | fable | inherit | full ID), permissionMode, maxTurns, memory (user | project | local), skills, mcpServers, background, isolation: worktree, effort, hooks.</p></body></html></richcontent></node><node ID="ID_2072" TEXT="Built-ins: Explore (read-only), Plan (read-only), general-purpose (all tools). Explore/Plan skip…"><richcontent TYPE="NOTE"><html><head></head><body><p>Built-ins: Explore (read-only), Plan (read-only), general-purpose (all tools). Explore/Plan skip CLAUDE.md.</p></body></html></richcontent></node><node ID="ID_2073" TEXT="Fresh context: own system prompt, task message, CLAUDE.md, git snapshot, preloaded skills — NOT…"><richcontent TYPE="NOTE"><html><head></head><body><p>Fresh context: own system prompt, task message, CLAUDE.md, git snapshot, preloaded skills — NOT the parent's conversation, auto memory or output style. Forks (/fork) inherit everything.</p></body></html></richcontent></node><node ID="ID_2074" TEXT="Nesting allowed: default max depth 3; concurrency limit configurable. Invoke by natural…"><richcontent TYPE="NOTE"><html><head></head><body><p>Nesting allowed: default max depth 3; concurrency limit configurable. Invoke by natural language, @agent-name (guaranteed), claude --agent name, or 'agent' in settings. Completed subagents return an ID and can be resumed.</p></body></html></richcontent></node><node ID="ID_2075" TEXT="Warning when combined agent descriptions exceed 15,000 tokens; /tasks lists running subagents."></node></node><node ID="ID_2080" TEXT="⚠ Exam traps"><node ID="ID_2077" TEXT="Project .claude/agents/ beats user ~/.claude/agents/ — the opposite of skills (personal beats project)."></node><node ID="ID_2078" TEXT="Subagents don't see the parent's history or auto memory, but they do load CLAUDE.md (except Explore/Plan)."></node><node ID="ID_2079" TEXT="model: inherit uses the main model; omitting tools inherits all parent tools."></node></node><node ID="ID_2081" TEXT="{ } code"><richcontent TYPE="NOTE"><html><head></head><body><p>---</p><p>name: reviewer</p><p>description: Reviews code for error handling and security. Use proactively after edits under src/.</p><p>tools: Read, Glob, Grep, Bash</p><p>model: sonnet</p><p>memory: project</p><p>---</p><p>You are a strict senior reviewer. Report findings as file:line with a fix. Never edit files.</p></body></html></richcontent></node></node><node ID="ID_2096" TEXT="Claude Code — CLI reference (headless mode)" LINK="https://code.claude.com/docs/en/cli-reference"><richcontent TYPE="NOTE"><html><head></head><body><p>https://code.claude.com/docs/en/cli-reference</p></body></html></richcontent><node ID="ID_2090" TEXT="Key facts"><node ID="ID_2083" TEXT="claude (interactive); claude 'query'; claude -p 'query' (print/headless); cat file | claude -p;…"><richcontent TYPE="NOTE"><html><head></head><body><p>claude (interactive); claude 'query'; claude -p 'query' (print/headless); cat file | claude -p; -c/--continue (most recent session); -r/--resume &lt;id|name&gt;; claude update; claude doctor; claude mcp; claude plugin.</p></body></html></richcontent></node><node ID="ID_2084" TEXT="Output: --output-format text | json | stream-json; --input-format stream-json;…"><richcontent TYPE="NOTE"><html><head></head><body><p>Output: --output-format text | json | stream-json; --input-format stream-json; --include-partial-messages (stream-json only); --json-schema for validated structured output; --verbose. JSON output includes result, cost, usage, session_id.</p></body></html></richcontent></node><node ID="ID_2085" TEXT="Permissions: --permission-mode default|acceptEdits|plan|auto|dontAsk|bypassPermissions;…"><richcontent TYPE="NOTE"><html><head></head><body><p>Permissions: --permission-mode default|acceptEdits|plan|auto|dontAsk|bypassPermissions; --dangerously-skip-permissions; --allowedTools / --disallowedTools; --add-dir; --permission-prompt-tool &lt;mcp tool&gt;.</p></body></html></richcontent></node><node ID="ID_2086" TEXT="Prompts: --system-prompt REPLACES the default; --append-system-prompt adds to it. --settings…"><richcontent TYPE="NOTE"><html><head></head><body><p>Prompts: --system-prompt REPLACES the default; --append-system-prompt adds to it. --settings &lt;file|json&gt;; --setting-sources user,project,local; --agents '{…}'.</p></body></html></richcontent></node><node ID="ID_2087" TEXT="Limits: --max-turns N (print mode only); --max-budget-usd; --model; --effort; --fallback-model…"><richcontent TYPE="NOTE"><html><head></head><body><p>Limits: --max-turns N (print mode only); --max-budget-usd; --model; --effort; --fallback-model a,b. Sessions: --session-id, --fork-session, --name.</p></body></html></richcontent></node><node ID="ID_2088" TEXT="MCP: --mcp-config &lt;file|json&gt;; --strict-mcp-config (only those servers). --bare skips…"><richcontent TYPE="NOTE"><html><head></head><body><p>MCP: --mcp-config &lt;file|json&gt;; --strict-mcp-config (only those servers). --bare skips hooks/skills/plugins/MCP; --safe-mode disables customisations.</p></body></html></richcontent></node><node ID="ID_2089" TEXT="-p runs default to permission mode 'default' and skip trust verification."></node></node><node ID="ID_2094" TEXT="⚠ Exam traps"><node ID="ID_2091" TEXT="--system-prompt replaces the whole default prompt; --append-system-prompt adds to it."></node><node ID="ID_2092" TEXT="--max-turns applies only in print (-p) mode."></node><node ID="ID_2093" TEXT="--strict-mcp-config ignores every configured server except those passed via --mcp-config."></node></node><node ID="ID_2095" TEXT="{ } code"><richcontent TYPE="NOTE"><html><head></head><body><p>cat app.log | claude -p --output-format json --max-turns 3 \</p><p>  --permission-mode plan &quot;Find critical errors and summarise&quot;</p><p>claude -p &quot;review this diff&quot; --allowedTools &quot;Read,Grep&quot; &lt; pr.diff</p><p>claude -r &quot;auth-refactor&quot; --append-system-prompt &quot;Always suggest tests&quot;</p></body></html></richcontent></node></node><node ID="ID_2109" TEXT="Claude Code — GitHub Actions" LINK="https://code.claude.com/docs/en/github-actions"><richcontent TYPE="NOTE"><html><head></head><body><p>https://code.claude.com/docs/en/github-actions</p></body></html></richcontent><node ID="ID_2103" TEXT="Key facts"><node ID="ID_2097" TEXT="Action anthropics/claude-code-action@v1. Quick setup: /install-github-app (needs gh CLI and repo…"><richcontent TYPE="NOTE"><html><head></head><body><p>Action anthropics/claude-code-action@v1. Quick setup: /install-github-app (needs gh CLI and repo admin); manual: install the Claude GitHub App + secret + copy the example workflow to .github/workflows/.</p></body></html></richcontent></node><node ID="ID_2098" TEXT="Auth inputs: anthropic_api_key (ANTHROPIC_API_KEY secret) or claude_code_oauth_token (from…"><richcontent TYPE="NOTE"><html><head></head><body><p>Auth inputs: anthropic_api_key (ANTHROPIC_API_KEY secret) or claude_code_oauth_token (from claude setup-token); use_bedrock / use_vertex / use_foundry for cloud platforms.</p></body></html></richcontent></node><node ID="ID_2099" TEXT="Modes are auto-detected: interactive (no prompt → waits for the trigger phrase, default @claude)…"><richcontent TYPE="NOTE"><html><head></head><body><p>Modes are auto-detected: interactive (no prompt → waits for the trigger phrase, default @claude) vs automation (prompt given → runs on any event). There is no mode input in v1.</p></body></html></richcontent></node><node ID="ID_2100" TEXT="Trigger gates: the actor needs write access; bots rejected unless allow-listed. Workflow…"><richcontent TYPE="NOTE"><html><head></head><body><p>Trigger gates: the actor needs write access; bots rejected unless allow-listed. Workflow permissions: contents, pull-requests, issues write; id-token: write (required for app auth); actions: read for CI results.</p></body></html></richcontent></node><node ID="ID_2101" TEXT="Inputs: prompt, claude_args (any CLI flag: --max-turns, --model, --allowedTools, --mcp-config),…"><richcontent TYPE="NOTE"><html><head></head><body><p>Inputs: prompt, claude_args (any CLI flag: --max-turns, --model, --allowedTools, --mcp-config), settings, plugins, github_token. Plain-text prompts get no shell/GitHub tools until granted via --allowedTools or settings.</p></body></html></richcontent></node><node ID="ID_2102" TEXT="Commits made with the default GITHUB_TOKEN don't trigger CI — omit github_token so it…"><richcontent TYPE="NOTE"><html><head></head><body><p>Commits made with the default GITHUB_TOKEN don't trigger CI — omit github_token so it authenticates as the app. Fork PRs on public repos don't get secrets. Costs: Actions minutes + API tokens; cap with --max-turns, timeouts, concurrency.</p></body></html></richcontent></node></node><node ID="ID_2107" TEXT="⚠ Exam traps"><node ID="ID_2104" TEXT="Providing prompt switches the action to automation mode."></node><node ID="ID_2105" TEXT="id-token: write is required even without cloud-provider OIDC."></node><node ID="ID_2106" TEXT="Same-repo branches only — fork PRs on public repos get no secrets."></node></node><node ID="ID_2108" TEXT="{ } code"><richcontent TYPE="NOTE"><html><head></head><body><p>on:</p><p>  pull_request: {types: [opened, synchronize]}</p><p>jobs:</p><p>  review:</p><p>    runs-on: ubuntu-latest</p><p>    permissions: {contents: read, pull-requests: write, issues: write, id-token: write}</p><p>    steps:</p><p>      - uses: actions/checkout@v6</p><p>      - uses: anthropics/claude-code-action@v1</p><p>        with:</p><p>          anthropic_api_key: ${{ secrets.ANTHROPIC_API_KEY }}</p><p>          prompt: &quot;Review this PR for error handling and security. Comment inline.&quot;</p><p>          claude_args: &quot;--max-turns 8 --allowedTools Read,Grep,Glob&quot;</p></body></html></richcontent></node></node></node><node ID="ID_2131" TEXT="❓ Self-check"><node ID="ID_2112" TEXT="You want every file edit auto-formatted with black. CLAUDE.md instruction or hook?"><node ID="ID_2111" TEXT="→ PostToolUse hook on Edit|Write — deterministic."></node></node><node ID="ID_2114" TEXT="Context is getting long mid-task but you need to keep working. Command?"><node ID="ID_2113" TEXT="→ /compact (keeps a summary); /clear would lose the thread."></node></node><node ID="ID_2116" TEXT="Which file holds team-shared permissions and hooks?"><node ID="ID_2115" TEXT="→ .claude/settings.json (committed); settings.local.json is personal."></node></node><node ID="ID_2118" TEXT="What does a hook exit code 2 do?"><node ID="ID_2117" TEXT="→ Blocks the tool call and feeds stderr back to Claude as the reason."></node></node><node ID="ID_2120" TEXT="Where do you put a personal note about the project that must not be committed?"><node ID="ID_2119" TEXT="→ CLAUDE.local.md (git-ignored)."></node></node><node ID="ID_2122" TEXT="Slash command vs skill?"><node ID="ID_2121" TEXT="→ Command: user-invoked, explicit /name. Skill: model-invoked when its description matches; can bundle scripts."></node></node><node ID="ID_2124" TEXT="How do you run Claude Code in CI and parse the result?"><node ID="ID_2123" TEXT="→ claude -p with --output-format json; read result/cost/session_id; key from secrets."></node></node><node ID="ID_2126" TEXT="When is --dangerously-skip-permissions acceptable?"><node ID="ID_2125" TEXT="→ Only inside an isolated sandbox/container without real credentials."></node></node><node ID="ID_2128" TEXT="A subagent finished — what does the main session receive?"><node ID="ID_2127" TEXT="→ Its returned summary only; the subagent's context is separate."></node></node><node ID="ID_2130" TEXT="Which loads first: user CLAUDE.md or project CLAUDE.md, and which wins on conflict?"><node ID="ID_2129" TEXT="→ All are loaded; more specific (project, then local) takes precedence over user."></node></node></node><node ID="ID_2144" TEXT="⚠ Traps to drill"><node ID="ID_2133" TEXT="'Must always run the linter after edits' — CLAUDE.md or hook?"><node ID="ID_2132" TEXT="→ Hook (PostToolUse). CLAUDE.md is guidance; hooks are enforcement."></node></node><node ID="ID_2135" TEXT="/compact vs /clear?"><node ID="ID_2134" TEXT="→ /compact summarises and continues; /clear wipes the context."></node></node><node ID="ID_2137" TEXT="Which settings file is committed for the team?"><node ID="ID_2136" TEXT="→ .claude/settings.json. settings.local.json is personal; ~/.claude/settings.json is user-wide."></node></node><node ID="ID_2139" TEXT="Hook exit code that blocks?"><node ID="ID_2138" TEXT="→ 2 — stderr goes back to Claude. 0 continues."></node></node><node ID="ID_2141" TEXT="Subagent cost?"><node ID="ID_2140" TEXT="→ Extra tokens — separate context window; only a summary returns."></node></node><node ID="ID_2143" TEXT="bypassPermissions where?"><node ID="ID_2142" TEXT="→ Sandboxed containers only."></node></node></node><node ID="ID_2152" TEXT="🗒 Cheat sheet"><node ID="ID_2145" TEXT="Memory: ~/.claude/CLAUDE.md (user) → ./CLAUDE.md (project, committed) → ./CLAUDE.local.md (personal); @imports; /memory; /init"></node><node ID="ID_2146" TEXT="Settings precedence: managed &gt; CLI flags &gt; .claude/settings.local.json &gt; .claude/settings.json &gt; ~/.claude/settings.json"></node><node ID="ID_2147" TEXT="Extend: commands (.claude/commands, user-invoked, $ARGUMENTS) · skills (.claude/skills/*/SKILL.md, model-invoked) · hooks (settings, enforcement) · subagents (.claude/agents, own context) · MCP · plugins"></node><node ID="ID_2148" TEXT="Hooks: PreToolUse/PostToolUse/Stop/UserPromptSubmit/SessionStart/PreCompact…; JSON on stdin; exit 0 ok, exit 2 block (+stderr to Claude), exit 1 non-blocking; default timeout 600 s"></node><node ID="ID_2149" TEXT="Modes: default · acceptEdits · plan (read-only) · bypassPermissions (sandbox only); deny rules win"></node><node ID="ID_2150" TEXT="Headless: claude -p, --output-format json|stream-json, --allowedTools, --max-turns, --resume; GitHub Action anthropics/claude-code-action"></node><node ID="ID_2151" TEXT="/compact summarise · /clear wipe · /cost (=/usage) tokens+USD · /context · /model · /effort · /permissions · /mcp · /agents · /review (=/code-review) · /resume · /fork"></node></node><node ID="ID_2160" TEXT="☑ Chapter checklist"><node ID="ID_2153" TEXT="Project CLAUDE.md committed and Claude Code follows it"></node><node ID="ID_2154" TEXT="One custom slash command and one skill in .claude/"></node><node ID="ID_2155" TEXT="A PostToolUse hook runs automatically; a PreToolUse hook blocks a dangerous command"></node><node ID="ID_2156" TEXT="Reviewer subagent exists and was used"></node><node ID="ID_2157" TEXT="Headless run works in GitHub Actions"></node><node ID="ID_2158" TEXT="Know the difference between /compact and /clear, and what /cost shows"></node><node ID="ID_2159" TEXT="notes/claude-code.md written"></node></node></node>
